  {
    "index": 9,
    "hash": "vB0zMTx8IJRQt/w+nlJ97B961Jk=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T15:11:59.911Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Authorization flow: (1) If AUTH_ENABLED=false, all access granted; (2) Validate bearer token, extract ETH address; (3) If address in ADMINS, full access; (4) If document unprotected, anyone reads, authenticated users write; (5) If protected, check explicit grants. Grants support direct user grants and inherited grants (drive -> folder -> document). Permission levels: READ (view), WRITE (edit, includes READ), ADMIN (manage permissions, includes WRITE). Configured via env vars (AUTH_ENABLED, ADMINS, DEFAULT_PROTECTION, DOCUMENT_PERMISSIONS_ENABLED) or `powerhouse.config.json`. Env vars override config file values.\n\n## Auth subgraph query surface\n\nThe authorization state is readable over GraphQL from `packages/reactor-api/src/graphql/auth/schema.graphql`:\n\n- `documentAccess(documentId: String!): DocumentAccessInfo!` (line 57)\n- `userDocumentPermissions: [DocumentPermissionEntry!]!` (line 63)\n- `canExecuteOperation(documentId: String!, operationType: String!): Boolean!` (line 73)\n\n## Group grants were retired, not renamed\n\n`packages/reactor-api/src/migrations/003_remove_group_tables.ts` drops the `Group`, `UserGroup`,\n`DocumentGroupPermission` and `OperationGroupPermission` tables. Its own header states the feature\n\"had no consumers and disclosed ACL/membership metadata (AUTH_REVIEW S-H3/S-H5); it is retired in\nfavor of direct user grants, ownership, and protection.\" Grepping `group` across\n`packages/reactor-api/src/graphql/auth/` returns zero hits. The surviving tables are three:\n`DocumentPermission`, `OperationUserPermission` (migration 001) and `DocumentProtection` (002).\n\n_Source-verified 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse source at v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T15:11:59.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T15:11:59.911Z"
    }
  },
